pergloss on al-Jurjani's Sharifiyya gloss on Shams al-Din al-Isfahani's older Sharh of Tajrid. The preface explicitly distinguishes this old-commentary base from Qushji's Sharh al-jadid. New work candidate; do not merge with W167 or with Dawani's 'qadima' gloss on Qushji.\n7. الحاشية على شرح القطبي للرسالة الشمسية → W204; Gloss on Qutb al-Din al-Razi's commentary on Najm al-Din Katibi's Shamsiyya. New work candidate; separate from Sadr's gloss on Qutb al-Razi's Sharh al-Matali.\n8. الحاشية على شرح مختصر الأصول → W205; Gloss on Iji's commentary on Mukhtasar al-usul (an abridged usul al-fiqh selection from Ibn al-Hajib). Candidate title is sourced from the preface; the exact base witness and its relation to the currently modelled debate need checking.\n9. حاشية على شرح المطالع (2 حاشية) → W202/W203; Two distinct Sadr glosses on Qutb al-Din al-Razi's Sharh al-Matali, a commentary on al-Urmawi's Matali al-anwar. The preface names the old and new Sadriyya glosses and says the latter answers Dawani's critique of the former. Item 4 is the second gloss with its fuller title, not a third Matali work.\n10. الحاشية على الكشاف للزمخشري → W244; Catalogue-listed gloss on al-Zamakhshari's al-Kashshaf. Preserve as a separate candidate if the parent inventory aims at the full bibliography; no core identity work was checked.\n11. الحاشية على المطول → W245; Gloss on al-Taftazani's al-Mutawwal, whose base is the Ma'ani wa-bayan portion of al-Khatib al-Dimashqi's Mukhtasar, itself an abridgment of al-Sakkaki's Miftah al-ulum. New candidate.\n12. رسالة في الفياض → W246; Short commentary on the word al-Fayyad at the beginning of Qutb al-Din al-Razi's Sharh al-Matali; the preface gives opening words. New candidate with an explicit relation to the Matali commentary tradition.\n13. رسالة في الكلام → W247; A separately listed theological treatise; the preface gives no content summary in the read lines. New candidate; title alone does not establish an identity with another kalam treatise.\n14. رسالة في خواص الجواهر → W248; Persian treatise on the types, properties, and value of minerals. The preface says Ghiyath's Kashf al-haqa'iq and Rihana attribute it to the elder Sadr, while Corbin assigns a similarly titled Jawhar-nama to Sadr II. Keep as tentative and do not merge with Sadr II's work.\n15. رساله‌ای در قوس قزح یا هاله یا خرمن ماه → W249; Persian text; the source supplies a descriptive label rather than a verified authorial title, and gives the opening: بعد از تيمن وتبرك به نام مبدعى كه به محض خود ذرات كائنات را از كتم عدم به شهرستان وجود فرستاد. Keep as an incipit-identified candidate, not an exact title.\n16. رسالة في الوجود الذهني → W250; Separate treatise on mental existence, discussed in the preface with Sadr's thesis and its later reception by Mulla Sadra. New candidate."}
